    "body": "## Independent exact-HEAD review - PR442 SQLite probe safety corrections\n\n**Reviewed HEAD:** `f1a4592e5b72c5d54d0f72c558dbc37c08b07733`, sole parent `f11dd978ca12f19b5c1f0463bf9d239521aa4eba`, tree `03ed5cc5b401d213afafc8102bf201ef0bfa4698`. Existing Draft PR442 remains OPEN/DRAFT/UNMERGED, clean/mergeable, exact PR441 base `6ad90e6e86d528b1858776477fb7e8680f89115d`; parent PR440 unchanged. Compared old-to-new 1 ahead, 0 behind, only the two authorized synthetic test files changed; compared to PR441 2 ahead, 0 behind, exactly these 2 files added.\n\n**Verdict: `PASS_NARROW_SQLITE_PROBE_SAFETY_CORRECTIONS` / previous R186 blockers CLOSED FOR THIS SYNTHETIC PROBE ONLY.**\n\n- `chat03b2_schema_v4_probe.sql`: all old `0003` creation rows now migrate to `CLOSED`, removing stored nonce/key version/ciphertext/generation from live rows. This does **not** assume the current `0002` token digests establish original issuance provenance. Fresh `RECOVERABLE` exists only as a post-migration synthetic fixture with explicit test generation 7, avoiding the unsafe prior legacy backfill.\n- `TOMBSTONE` now requires `request_fingerprint_sha256`, `battle_id`, deadline, `created_at_ms` and recovery material to be NULL; the idempotency SHA-256 digest, lifecycle label and nullable purge metadata remain. Tests explicitly assert all forbidden tombstone columns are null and demonstrate duplicate key refusal until a deliberately simulated purge.\n- Existing fixture still tests FK/row preservation, rollback on invalid transitions, dependent-row deletion, and selected two-connection SQLite transaction races. Tests visibly distinguish Python-only `simulate_participant_commit_transaction` and `simulate_scheduler_terminal_transaction` from real SQL Worker security.\n\n**Exact published HEAD CI independently verified including real job logs:** [CAS SQL #39960933558](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39960933558) `head_sha=f1a4592...`, SUCCESS, 39/39 Python tests with 17 distinct `Chat03B2SchemaV4ProbeTests` passing, local Wrangler checks plus retired runner 5/5; [Private API #39960933418](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39960933418) same HEAD SUCCESS, offline safety 22/22 and original private local workerd integration PASS; [Forensics #39960933431](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39960933431) same HEAD SUCCESS. All first attempts. Codex additionally reports direct probe 44 positive / 18 negative and local policy/diff checks; those totals/checks were not separately executed by this reviewer.\n\n**Preserved limits:** The test fixture is not deployable migration `0004`. Migration 0002 still has no actual capability `generation` column or original-issued-token provenance, the existing Worker is not generation-aware or SQL revocation-fenced, and v4 synthetic transitions are Python simulations. No real D1 hosted concurrency, Cloudflare, deployment, real-human access policy, keyring restore or main merge approved.\n\n**PR description warning:** the GitHub PR body still describes the previous unsafe synthetic `generation=1` backfill and earlier behavior. The authoritative source for this verdict is exact HEAD/code and this review. Its metadata edit was denied in the Codex task; this reviewer has **not** modified PR title/body or bypassed that restriction. Any future body update should be separately authorized.\n\n**Next step:** after this independent review, plan a separate narrowly scoped, synthetic/local-only generation-aware capability lifecycle implementation/proof, with user-approved checkpoint+recovery and fresh clean branch. Do not edit or merge existing PRs without separate scope/authority.",
